Recently, I made the following bug (buggy code is old, fixed code is new):
diff --git a/torch/lib/THS/generic/THSTensor.c b/torch/lib/THS/generic/THSTensor.c
index ce24a86..0d5d3e0 100644
--- a/torch/lib/THS/generic/THSTensor.c
+++ b/torch/lib/THS/generic/THSTensor.c
@@ -191,8 +191,8 @@ THSTensor *THSTensor_(newWithTensorAndSize)(THLongTensor *indices, THTensor *val
   }
   // NB: by default, we do NOT clone indices/values into the sparse tensor.
   // Efficient API by default!
-  THSTensor_(retain)(indices);
-  THSTensor_(retain)(values);
+  THLongTensor_retain(indices);
+  THTensor_(retain)(values);
   THSTensor_(_move)(self, indices, values);

   return self;

What I found perplexing is that gcc didn't error out when I made this mistake. Instead, it emitted a warning only:
In file included from generic/THSTensor.c:2:0,
                 from /home/ezyang/local/pytorch/torch/lib/THS/THSTensor.c:4:
/home/ezyang/local/pytorch/torch/lib/THS/generic/THSTensor.c: In function ‘THSByteTensor_newWithTenso
rAndSize’:
/home/ezyang/local/pytorch/torch/lib/THS/generic/THSTensor.c:194:3: warning: passing argument 1 of ‘T
HSByteTensor_retain’ from incompatible pointer type [enabled by default]
   THSTensor_(retain)(indices);
   ^
In file included from /home/ezyang/local/pytorch/torch/lib/tmp_install/include/TH/TH.h:4:0,
                 from /home/ezyang/local/pytorch/torch/lib/THS/THSTensor.h:4,
                 from /home/ezyang/local/pytorch/torch/lib/THS/THSTensor.c:1:
/home/ezyang/local/pytorch/torch/lib/THS/THSTensor.h:8:40: note: expected ‘struct THSByteTensor *’ bu
t argument is of type ‘struct THLongTensor *’
 #define THSTensor_(NAME)   TH_CONCAT_4(THS,Real,Tensor_,NAME)
                                        ^
/home/ezyang/local/pytorch/torch/lib/tmp_install/include/TH/THGeneral.h:109:37: note: in definition o
f macro ‘TH_CONCAT_4_EXPAND’
 #define TH_CONCAT_4_EXPAND(x,y,z,w) x ## y ## z ## w
                                     ^
/home/ezyang/local/pytorch/torch/lib/THS/THSTensor.h:8:28: note: in expansion of macro ‘TH_CONCAT_4’
 #define THSTensor_(NAME)   TH_CONCAT_4(THS,Real,Tensor_,NAME)
                            ^
/home/ezyang/local/pytorch/torch/lib/THS/generic/THSTensor.h:67:13: note: in expansion of macro ‘THST
ensor_’
 TH_API void THSTensor_(retain)(THSTensor *self);
             ^

It would really be great if we can turn this into an honest-to-goodness error. The usual thing to do is -Werror but I have noticed that we are NOT warnings clean, and I don't know how much effort it would be to make it so.
If try to Werror JUST these warnings, we will need GCC and Clang specific incants. As far as I can tell, for clang, it's -Werror=incompatible-pointer-types; for GCC it's -Werror=strict-aliasing but only if your GCC is sufficiently recent.
